            <ArticleTitle>An improved radiant heat algometer and its application to pain threshold measurements in man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A radiant heat algometer system is described which enables the psychophysical and clinical study of cutaneous pain sensations and reactions by means of a precise, stabilized power source. In this system DC electric power consumption of a bulb is automatically controlled, and no calibration is necessary to be controlled frequently. Moreover, attention is drawn to the significance of using the blackened sticky tape and of the pre-heating procedure. The application of this algometer is also described for a pain threshold determination with the intensity and time methods.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
